            "review_title": "Review at Vinh Nghiem",
            "review_text": "David A\nBroadstone, United Kingdom95 contributions\n0\nBest meals we ever had in Vietnam\nJan 2018 • Friends\nIf you haven't eaten at any of the vegetarian or vegan restaurants in Vietnam then I do recommend you try them out for a delicious and varied meal - even if you are not a vegan or vegetarian yourself. In the UK a vegetarian meal either consists of some uninspiring dishes with cheese, mushroom, nuts or similar, such as goats cheese tart, mushroom risotto, stuffed peppers, nut roast etc. This restaurant is in a different class to the UK vegan/vegetarian restaurant and puts most other restaurants in Saigon to shame - even those that are non-vegan/vegetarian.\n\nThe restaurant is within the Vinh Nghiem pagoda (Buddhist temple) compound, so why not make the most of it - visit the pagoda and have a great meal in the restaurant.\n\nThe menu is practically impossible to understand (unless you ask for the English version) apart from a few photographs, but some of the waiters and waitresses speak English and are quite helpful.\n\nWe have had breakfasts a number of times there and also lunch and dinner, and each time was a different experience. As we were travelling with Vietnamese friends, they chose most of the time and we made a few tentative choices which always turned out great, although sometimes a bit unexpected!\nRead more\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 24, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
